        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: keep command cron jobs operator-scoped [AI]",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where agent-runtime cron callers could inspect or manually trigger operator-created command cron jobs when those jobs were routed to the same agent.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nGateway cron caller scoping now treats command-payload and on-exit cron jobs as operator-only whenever the request comes from an internal agent-runtime identity. Operator and admin Gateway calls without that identity continue to use the existing cron management paths.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can keep command cron automation configured for an agent without making those command details or manual run controls available through the model-visible cron workflow. Normal agent-authored reminder and agent-turn cron jobs remain visible to the owning agent.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAI-assisted.\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- AWS Crabbox `run_6432090bdaf0` on `cbx_4469d6f0abd0`: `corepack pnpm test src/gateway/server-methods/cron.validation.test.ts`\n- Result: 2 Gateway Vitest shards passed, 204 assertions passed.\n",
